In a browser, the user clicks `btn`. What is logged?
```js
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  setTimeout(() => console.log('timeout'));
  console.log('L1');
});
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  console.log('L2');
});
```

In Node, what does this log?
```js
import { EventEmitter } from 'node:events';
const e = new EventEmitter();
e.on('go', () => {
  setTimeout(() => console.log('timeout'));
  console.log('L1');
});
e.on('go', () => console.log('L2'));
e.emit('go');
console.log('after');
```

What does the user see after clicking?
```js
btn.onclick = () => {
  spinner.hidden = false;
  crunch(); // 2 s, synchronous
  spinner.hidden = true;
};
```

Inside one click handler, this runs for about 2 s. What does the user see?
